course: dictionary
lesson: 11245
title: Words that taste of feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing, and some words describe how something feels. Wormwood can do both. It is the name of a plant with silvery-grey leaves and a very bitter taste.
explain: «The defeat was wormwood to him.» A defeat is not a plant, so the word must mean something else. A defeat can leave a bitter, painful feeling, so wormwood here means something very bitter or painful to bear.
explain: Use the clues around the word. In «gall and wormwood», both words are bitter things, so the phrase means great bitterness. To check, put your meaning in the sentence: "The defeat was very bitter to him" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Wormwood is a plant with silvery-grey leaves and a very bitter taste.
fact: «Wormwood» can also mean something very bitter or painful to bear.
fact: «Gall and wormwood» means great bitterness.
fact: Long ago, wormwood was used in medicine and in some strong drinks.
fact: In the Bible, wormwood stands for bitterness and sorrow.
exercise: «The defeat was wormwood to him.» In this sentence, what does wormwood mean? | A sweet and sticky medicine | *Something very bitter or painful to bear | A cold, windy day | A tall tree that grows near rivers
exercise: What does the phrase «gall and wormwood» suggest? | *Great bitterness | Happy singing | A cool breeze | Sweet dreams
exercise: Long ago, people used wormwood as a | building material for castles | pet food | *medicine | mobile phone
test: A poem says, «Those lonely days were wormwood to her.» What does this suggest? | *Painful and bitter days | Days full of games | Quiet and peaceful days | Warm and sunny days
test: What kind of taste does the wormwood plant have? | Sour, like a lemon | *Very bitter | Sweet, like honey | Salty, like the sea
exam: What does wormwood mean in the phrase «as bitter as wormwood»? | Very cold | Very sweet | *Very bitter | Very loud
